# Netlify redirects for the SPA cutover. Single source for redirects: netlify.toml
# has no [[redirects]] block, so there is one precedence order to reason about.
# Vite copies this file into the publish root.
#
# Rules are matched in order. A trailing "!" forces the rule even when a file exists.
# 302 (not 301) until production is verified, so rollback is not blocked by cached 301s.
# Each redirected static page has a .html rule and a pretty-URL rule, because Netlify
# serves /foundation/staff/x without the extension.

# Entry points
/                                                        /foundation/auth/login.html        302!
/auth                                                    /auth/login                        302!
/staff                                                   /staff/admin-portal                302!

# Legacy static auth URLs: the SPA owns /auth/* (login and reset-password)
/auth/login.html                                         /auth/login                        302!
/auth/reset-password.html                                /auth/reset-password               302!
/foundation/staff/login.html                             /foundation/auth/login.html        302!
/foundation/staff/login                                  /foundation/auth/login.html        302!

